  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `camcraft_motion::machining2d::slot_centre_band` (new file `crates/motion/src/machining2d/slot_band.rs`) holds the slot fit rule: `h = width / 2 - r - leave`, and `h = 0` is permitted. The slot generator (`slots.rs`) and the commands call it. There is no second copy of the rule.\n- `slot_gate` (`crates/app/src/commands/operation/gates.rs`) is separate from `tool_gate`. It takes the setup and the source. It runs in these commands:\n  - `CreateOperation`;\n  - `EditOperationLinks` (MCP `set_tool`, the UI links edit), only when the tool changes;\n  - `ChangeOperationKind`.\n- The gate refuses a plain Slot whose tool is too wide. The UI shows the same text after its `links not updated: ` prefix.\n- The default width. `operation::seed_slot_for_tool` (`crates/app/src/operation/slot_pick.rs`) sets the width of a new Slot from the seed to the larger of 4 mm and the tool diameter. It runs at three doors:\n  - the ribbon quick-add (`crates/ui/src/actions.rs`, beside `seed_helix_for_tool`);\n  - MCP `add_operation`, before the params patch (`crates/app/src/mcp/edit.rs`);\n  - the change of kind (`ChangeOperationKind`, after `retype_params`).\n- A tool of 4 mm or less gives the same operation as before. A width that the caller or the picks state is not changed, and the gate judges it.\n- Picks that seed no slot. If `slot_from_picks` is `None`, the width is only the seed fallback. `operation::slot_width_is_stated` is then false, and the gate does not judge the width. Generate keeps its pick refusal (for example \"is not a slot outline\").\n- `ChangeTool` (the second door, MCP `tool_edit`) refuses a diameter edit that makes the tool too wide for a plain Slot that uses it (`operation::tool_gate::resize_refusal`). It checks only when the diameter increases, and it skips operations whose picks seed no slot.\n- The text is in `operation::tool_gate::slot_fit_refusal`. It uses the document unit (`units::len`) and has no G-code words.\n- The generator keeps its own refusal. A project file from an older build can still hold the bad pair.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/3475-tool-fit-at-edit.md`.\n\n## The refusal text\n\nBefore: `CreateOperation` and `set_tool` accepted the tool. Generate refused later with \"slot is narrower than the tool: the slot is 3.000 mm wide (0.000 mm left on each wall) and the tool is 4.000 mm\".\n\nAfter, at the command:\n\n```\ninvalid parameters: the tool 'EM-WIDE' is 10 mm wide and the slot is 6 mm wide: choose a tool of 6 mm or less\ninvalid parameters: the tool 'EM-SIX' is 6 mm wide and the slot is 6 mm wide with 0.5 mm left on each wall: choose a tool of 5 mm or less\ninvalid parameters: S1 uses it: the tool 'EM-0400-2FL' is 100 mm wide and the slot is 6 mm wide: choose a tool of 6 mm or less\n```\n\nMCP adds its usual `set_tool: ` prefix. In an inch document the sizes are in inches.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` lib, `machining2d::slot_band::tests` (5 tests): fits, equal width, too wide, stock to leave makes it too wide, NaN / infinite / zero / negative refused cleanly.\n- `camcraft-app` `--test slot_tool_fit` (new file, 7 tests):\n  - `a_wide_tool_on_a_slot_is_refused_at_set_tool_and_changes_nothing` (the tool and the undo stack do not change);\n  - `a_tool_that_fits_is_accepted`;\n  - `a_wide_tool_on_a_slot_is_refused_at_create`;\n  - `stock_to_leave_is_part_of_the_fit`;\n  - `the_sentence_follows_the_document_unit`;\n  - `a_tool_library_edit_that_widens_a_slot_cutter_is_refused`;\n  - `a_change_of_kind_to_slot_holds_the_ops_own_tool` (a 10 mm tool gives width 10; a 4 mm tool keeps 4).\n- `camcraft-app` `--test mcp`, new module `mcp/slot_tool_fit.rs` (2 tests):\n  - `slot_tool_fit::set_tool_refuses_a_tool_wider_than_the_slot_without_mutation` (through `Client::refused`; `get_job` is the same after the refusal; an explicit width of 4 with a 6 mm tool is refused at `add_operation`);\n  - `slot_tool_fit::add_operation_seeds_the_slot_width_from_the_tool` (a 6 mm tool gives width 6; a 3 mm tool keeps 4).\n- `camcraft-app` `--test slot_dxf_sketch` (5 tests), new test `picks_that_are_no_slot_keep_their_pick_refusal_under_a_wider_tool`: a 6 mm tool on a rectangle pick is accepted at create, and generate refuses with \"is not a slot outline\".\n- UI: no UI test was added. No UI test for a refused tool assignment exists to copy. The UI calls the same commands and the same seed function as MCP.\n\n## Changed test\n\n`slot_dxf_sketch::picks_that_are_no_slot_are_refused_by_name`, the plain Slot on the 3 mm outline with the 4 mm tool:\n\n- Old: `CreateOperation` is accepted. `GenerateOperation` refuses with \"slot is narrower than the tool\" and \"3.000 mm\", \"4.000 mm\".\n- New: `CreateOperation` refuses with \"is 4 mm wide and the slot is 3 mm wide: choose a tool of 3 mm or less\".\n\nThe Trochoidal Slot case did not change.\n\n## Gate (head `bdafcfc4c`, debug, `-j 6`)\n\n- motion `--lib` 556 pass.\n- app `--lib` 300; `slot_tool_fit` 7; `slot_dxf_sketch` 5; `tilt_a180` 2; `slot_extension` 5; `tilt_heights` 8; `setup_align_2d_kinds` 8; `wcs_rotation_control` 5; `pocket_recognition` 11; `tool_gate` 10; `tool_law` 5; `mcp` 29; `mcp_doc_drift` 6; `operations` 121; `golden_cl` 33; `conformance` 7; `docs_troubleshooting` 1; `example_catalog` 37; `example_catalog_adaptive` 1; `example_catalog_edge_work` 1; `first_part_programs` 2. All pass.\n- `camcraft-ui --lib` 1494 pass. Each integration binary under `crates/ui/tests` passes (23 binaries, including `operations` 31, `shell` 21, `egui_app` 8).\n- clippy `-D warnings`: motion `--all-targets`; app `--lib --test slot_tool_fit --test mcp --test slot_dxf_sketch`; ui `--all-targets`. All clean.\n\n## Not run\n\n- No heavy lane and no light lane (P3).\n- The app window was not started.\n\n## What remains (follow-up #3631)\n\n- 2D Pocket. Its fit needs the region that the generator cuts: the containment, the stock and the part slice. The command does not have that region, and an estimate can refuse legal work. #3631 (P3, area:mcp, effort:high) holds the pocket warning.\n- The command does not refuse a Slot width edit (`EditOperationParams`) below the current tool yet. #3631 holds it too.\n- The MCP reply shape of `set_tool` did not change, so `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` did not change. The `camcraft-mcp` skill row for `set_tool` can name the slot width rule. That skill is a process file, and the row is owed.\n\nChangelog: A tool wider than a plain Slot is now refused when it is assigned (create, `set_tool`, the links edit, a change of kind) or made wider in the tool library, with both sizes and the largest tool that fits; a new Slot from the default is at least as wide as its tool.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nRefs #3475\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
